
This directory holds the runtime library modules for the native
code implementation of BCPL for Raspberry Pi machines using the ARMv7
architecture. It uses 32-bit registers and execute essentially the the
original ARM machine code

These libraries and the codegenerator (now called com/bcplcgarmv7.b)
were implemented by D.J.Allerton with minor modifications by
M.Richards to allow them to run under modern Cintcode BCPL. What is
planned is both a cross compiler running on the Cintcode BCPL system
and a native code version of the compiler running directly on an ARMv7
Raspbe rry Pi such as the Model 2B.

This is still under development. Initially this system will be limited
to 32-bit BCPL and will not compile the floating point operators and
constants. But floating point will be available using the
sys(Sys_flt,...) facilities.

This directory is called BCPL/cintcode/armv7. The version for later
Raspberry PIs running ARMv8, typically called Model 3, 4 and 5, is
directory BCPL/cintcode/armv8. This is still in early stages of
development.

MR
